  ],
  "justification": "The customer scenario describes a small independent charity receiving donations via direct debit and one-off donations, but provides no information about whether the charity is recognised as a charity or CASC for tax purposes, whether donors have paid sufficient tax, whether Gift Aid declarations have been made, or the nature of the donations. Without these facts, the conditions for Gift Aid eligibility as specified in E02, E04, E05, E09, E10, E11, E12, and E13 cannot be verified. The intermediate representation incorrectly assumes these facts are established based on the scenario, but the evidence does not support them.",
  "missing_facts": [
    "Whether the charity is recognised as a charity or CASC for tax purposes",
    "Whether each donor has paid at least as much in Income Tax or Capital Gains Tax in the relevant tax year as the amount of Gift Aid being claimed",
    "Whether each donor has made a Gift Aid declaration",
    "Whether the donations (direct debits or one-off) are made through Payroll Giving",
    "Whether the donations are payments for goods or services or made because the charity or CASC bought goods and services",
    "Whether the donor receives a benefit over a certain limit",
    "Whether the donation is shares",
    "Whether the donation is from charity cards or vouchers such as CAF vouchers"
  ],
  "scope_issues": [
    "The policy does not specify whether the conditions apply to one-off donations or recurring donations such as monthly direct debits, creating a scope ambiguity in the application of Gift Aid rules to different types of donations."
  ],
